# Temporal Knowledge

Spec: TemporalKnowledge
Purpose:
  Define how temporal knowledge (valid_from / valid_until) is recorded,
  queried, and reconciled. Temporal awareness lets AI answer historical
  context questions without creating duplicate concepts for each era.

Owns: timeline/changes.sdd

Temporal Validity:
  Every time-sensitive knowledge entry MUST carry:
    valid_from: timestamp when the entry became valid
    valid_until: timestamp when the entry was superseded (or "now")

  Example:
    @architecture.modular-monolith
    valid:
      2026-01-01 → 2027-06-15

    @architecture.microservices
    valid:
      2027-06-15 → now

Versioning Policy:
  Versioning is NOT based on file edits. Version increments only occur on
  semantic changes. Cosmetic changes (typo, formatting, comment) do NOT
  trigger a version bump.

  Semantic change triggers:
    - architecture changed
    - decision changed
    - skill behavior changed
    - policy changed
    - constraint added or removed

Semantic Change Classification:
  COSMETIC      — typo, formatting, comment only
  CONTENT       — factual information added/removed
  SEMANTIC      — meaning changed (same structure, different interpretation)
  BEHAVIORAL    — skill/decision behavior changed
  ARCHITECTURAL — architecture pattern or boundary changed
  POLICY        — rules or governance changed

  Example:
    "Use PostgreSQL" → "Use PostgreSQL for transactional data"
    → SEMANTIC_CHANGE

    "PostgreSQL" → "PostgreSQL "
    → COSMETIC (formatting only)

Version Semantics (MAJOR.MINOR.PATCH):
  MAJOR → behavior/contract significantly changed
  MINOR → new capability added (backward compatible)
  PATCH → correction/improvement (backward compatible)

  Example:
    @skill.code-review v3.2.1

Skill Evolution:
  Skills evolve through versions. Existing tasks are NOT automatically
  upgraded to newer versions. This preserves historical reproducibility.

  Task context pins specific versions:
    skills:
      code-review@1.0
      ddd@2.1

  This is the snapshot of the task's environment.

State: +
